	"is_virtual": false,
	"identifying_description": "A mantle for a married woman above the age of 40, as signified by the egg-yolk yellow ground. The polychrome silk embroidery uses more green than usual and is very beautifully executed on the back of the garment, whereas the embroidery on the two fronts is clumsier, with elements differently spaced on left and right. The differences in embroidery suggest that three different women did the embroidery on this example. The cotton lining is coarsely woven and of Central Asian production.",
